-- Q3930: Individual Tax Planning: Compensation [easy/L1]
-- Issues: #3
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (D): Under IRC Sec. 83(a), RSUs are taxed as ordinary income when they vest and shares are delivered. The taxable amount equals the FMV of the shares on the vesting date, reported on the employee''s W-2. A Section 83(b) election is not available for RSUs because no property is transferred at grant.
Wrong (A): RSUs are not taxed at grant because no property has been transferred. The employee holds only a contractual promise until vesting.
Wrong (B): RSUs are not tax-free until sale. Income is recognized at vesting, and any subsequent gain or loss on sale is separate capital gain or loss.
Wrong (C): RSU income at vesting is ordinary income, not capital gain. Capital gain treatment applies only to post-vesting appreciation held beyond one year.$EXPL$
