-- Q3956: Individual Tax Planning: Compensation [medium/L2]
-- Issues: #3
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (D): Under IRC Sec. 409A and Rev. Proc. 92-64, rabbi trust assets remain subject to the employer''s general creditors upon insolvency. In bankruptcy, the executive becomes an unsecured general creditor with no priority over other creditors. This creditor exposure is the trade-off for deferring income recognition.
Wrong (A): The deferred amounts are not protected. Rabbi trust assets are available to all general creditors, so scheduled payments may not be made.
Wrong (B): The executive has no priority claim. Rabbi trust participants are treated as unsecured general creditors in bankruptcy proceedings.
